/-
# Conway–Sloane, Ch. 15, §9.5: Theorem 18 when the integral automorphisms are products of integral reflections

J. H. Conway and N. J. A. Sloane, *Sphere Packings, Lattices and Groups*, 3rd ed., Ch. 15, §9.5, p. 391
(`conwaysloane1999`), Theorem 18 and the remark after it: *for odd $p$ every $p$-adically integral automorphism is the
product of $p$-adically integral reflections. For $p = 2$ this is usually true but not always [O'Meara 1958].*

**Layer.** As in `Section9Theorem18Odd.lean`: a finite prime $\mathfrak p$ of a number field $F$, the form $Q$ on
$F_\mathfrak p^n$, a lattice $L$ with localization $L_\mathfrak p$, the integral automorphisms $O(L_\mathfrak p)$
(`locStabV`), the $p$-adic root vectors (`IsRootVector`: $Q(x) \ne 0$ and the reflection $\tau_x$ lies in
$O(L_\mathfrak p)$), and $\theta(O^+(L_\mathfrak p))$ = `localSpinorNormGroup`.

**Proves**
* `GeneratedByRootReflections`: the condition of the book's remark, every $\sigma \in O(L_\mathfrak p)$ is a product
  $\tau_{x_1}\cdots\tau_{x_r}$ of reflections in $p$-adic root vectors; `generatedByRootReflections_of_odd`: it holds
  for $\mathfrak p \nmid 2$ (Cassels, p. 115, Cor. 1; O'Meara 92:4).
* `theorem18_of_generated` (**Theorem 18 at every prime, including $p = 2$, under this condition**): $A \in
  \theta(O^+(L_\mathfrak p))$ if and only if $A$ is, up to squares, the product of the norms of an even number of
  $p$-adic root vectors.

At $p = 2$ the condition can fail (O'Meara 1958, O'Meara–Pollak 1965), and the general case is the named statement
`Theorem18Dyadic`. This file isolates exactly what the book's proof route needs: Theorem 18 at $p = 2$ holds for every
lattice $L$ whose $2$-adic integral automorphisms are generated by integral reflections.
-/
import QuadFormsKB.Literature.ConwaySloane.Section9Theorem18Odd

open NumberField IsDedekindDomain Matrix

set_option linter.unusedSectionVars false

noncomputable section

namespace QuadFormsKB.ConwaySloane

open Lattices

variable {F : Type} [Field F] [NumberField F] {n : ℕ} (Q : QuadForm F n) {v : HeightOneSpectrum (𝓞 F)}

local notation "Fv" => v.adicCompletion F

/-- **The integral automorphisms of $L_\mathfrak p$ are products of integral reflections** (the condition of the remark
after Conway–Sloane's Theorem 18, p. 391): every $\sigma \in O(L_\mathfrak p)$ equals $\tau_{x_1}\cdots\tau_{x_r}$ for
$p$-adic root vectors $x_1, \dots, x_r$ of $L$ at $\mathfrak p$. -/
@[kb "conwaysloane1999" "Ch. 15, §9.5, p. 391 (remark after Thm. 18: integral automorphisms are products of integral reflections)"]
def GeneratedByRootReflections (v : HeightOneSpectrum (𝓞 F)) (L : Lat F n) : Prop :=
  ∀ σ : orthGroup Q (v.adicCompletion F), σ ∈ locStabV Q v L →
    ∃ l : List (Fin n → v.adicCompletion F), (∀ u ∈ l, IsRootVector Q L v u) ∧ σ = symmProd Q _ l

/-- At $\mathfrak p \nmid 2$ the condition holds for every lattice (Conway–Sloane's remark, p. 391, citing Cassels,
p. 115, Cor. 1; here from O'Meara 92:4, `exists_rootVectors_of_mem_locStabV`). -/
@[kb "conwaysloane1999" "Ch. 15, §9.5, p. 391 (remark: for odd p every p-adically integral automorphism is a product of p-adically integral reflections)"]
theorem generatedByRootReflections_of_odd (hQ : Q.Nondegenerate) (h2 : (2 : 𝓞 F) ∉ v.asIdeal) (L : Lat F n) :
    GeneratedByRootReflections Q v L :=
  fun _ hσ => exists_rootVectors_of_mem_locStabV Q hQ h2 L hσ

/-- **Conway–Sloane, Theorem 18, at every prime whose integral automorphisms are generated by integral reflections**
(§9.5, p. 391), both directions: if every $\sigma \in O(L_\mathfrak p)$ is a product of reflections in $p$-adic root
vectors (`GeneratedByRootReflections`; automatic for $\mathfrak p \nmid 2$, "usually but not always" true for
$\mathfrak p \mid 2$), then for $A \in F_\mathfrak p^\times$: $A \in \theta(O^+(L_\mathfrak p))$ if and only if
$A F_\mathfrak p^{\times 2} = Q(x_1)\cdots Q(x_r)F_\mathfrak p^{\times 2}$ for an even number $r$ of $p$-adic root
vectors $x_1, \dots, x_r$. -/
@[kb "conwaysloane1999" "Ch. 15, §9.5, Thm. 18, p. 391 (every p, when integral automorphisms are products of integral reflections)"]
theorem theorem18_of_generated (hQ : Q.Nondegenerate) (L : Lat F n) (hgen : GeneratedByRootReflections Q v L)
    (A : Fvˣ) :
    A ∈ localSpinorNormGroup Q hQ v L ↔
      ∃ xs : List (Fin n → Fv), Even xs.length ∧ (∀ x ∈ xs, IsRootVector Q L v x) ∧
        SqClass.mk A = sqClassOf (valProd Q Fv xs) := by
  constructor
  · intro hA
    rw [mem_localSpinorNormGroup] at hA
    obtain ⟨σ, ⟨hσL, hσ1⟩, hσθ⟩ := hA
    obtain ⟨l, hl, rfl⟩ := hgen σ hσL
    have hl0 : ∀ u ∈ l, Q.evalIn Fv u ≠ 0 := fun u hu => (hl u hu).1
    refine ⟨l, ?_, hl, ?_⟩
    · have hdet := Tamagawa.mem_soSub.mp hσ1
      rw [det_symmProd Q l hl0] at hdet
      by_contra hodd
      rw [Nat.not_even_iff_odd] at hodd
      rw [hodd.neg_one_pow] at hdet
      exact absurd hdet (by norm_num)
    · rw [← hσθ, spinorNorm_symmProd Q Fv hQ l hl0]
  · rintro ⟨xs, hev, hr, hA⟩
    exact mem_localSpinorNormGroup_of_rootVectors hQ xs hev hr A hA

end QuadFormsKB.ConwaySloane
